rectangle "nyx\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>" <<Boundary-bnl4>> {
  rectangle "nyx-sms\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>" <<Boundary-bnl4LXNtcw==>> {
    rectangle "==Physics adapter\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe Physics implementation of sms with four studies (static, eigenfrequency, axisymmetric eigenfrequency, waveguide modes): descriptors, validation, solve entry." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxsms.Physicsadapter
    rectangle "==Typed problem\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nThe typed sms problem the kernels read, decoded from the envelope." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxsms.Typedproblem
    rectangle "==Solid kernel\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nLinear elastic solid mechanics on P1/P2 triangles and tetrahedra: static solve and eigenfrequencies." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxsms.Solidkernel
    rectangle "==Cross-section study kernel\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nCross-section study kernel (`axisymmetric_eigenfrequency` on the (r, z) half plane and 2.5D `modes` on the (x, z) cross-section): constraints, axis and periodic conditions, absorbing layers, complex eigensolve and fields; every mode carries numeric frequency parts, a layer fraction and its energy shares per component and domain." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxsms.Crosssectionstudykernel
    rectangle "==Axisymmetric kernel\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nElastic modes of a body of revolution on its half-plane cross-section, with the axis regularity conditions, the cylindrical PML stretch and the energy weight of a mode per component and class of cells." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxsms.Axisymmetrickernel
    rectangle "==Waveguide kernel\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nElastic modes of a 2.5D waveguide on its 2D (x, z) cross-section (`exp(-i q y)`), with full 3D anisotropic crystal orientation, planar PML coordinate stretching and the planar kinetic-energy weight of a mode per component and class of cells." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxsms.Waveguidekernel
    rectangle "==Floquet kernel\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nEigenfrequencies of a solid with Floquet-periodic boundaries (phononic crystals)." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxsms.Floquetkernel
    rectangle "==Absorbing-layer kernel\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nEigenfrequencies of elastic bodies with perfectly matched layers and optional Floquet-periodic boundaries." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxsms.Absorbinglayerkernel
    rectangle "==Low-reflecting boundary\n<size:16>[Component: Rust modules]</size>\n\nLow-reflecting boundaries for solid mechanics." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb21wb25lbnQ=>> as nyx.nyxsms.Lowreflectingboundary
  }

  component "==nyx-physics\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nThe Physics trait, the problem envelope (ProblemSpec), descriptors, SolveResult, the registry type, validation, JSON Schemas." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.nyxphysics
  component "==femcore\n<size:16>[Container: Rust library]</size>\n\nThe FEM core: meshes, meshing and adaptation, linear algebra behind one driver, finite-element basics, the material specification and library, expressions." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsTGlicmFyeQ==>> as nyx.femcore
}

